@startuml
title Figure 5.1 – RaSTA Architecture Based on the Black Channel Principle

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

rectangle "Safety-Related Railway System A" {

rectangle "Railway Application A" as APP_A

rectangle "RaSTA Sender Endpoint" {
  rectangle "CRC Generation"
  rectangle "Sequence Numbering"
  rectangle "Connection Supervision"
  rectangle "Endpoint Identification"
}
}

rectangle "Non-Safe Communication Network\nBlack Channel\n(Ethernet/IP/UDP)" as NET

rectangle "Safety-Related Railway System B" {

rectangle "RaSTA Receiver Endpoint" {
  rectangle "CRC Verification"
  rectangle "Sequence Verification"
  rectangle "Timeout Monitoring"
  rectangle "Endpoint Validation"
}

rectangle "Railway Application B" as APP_B
}

APP_A --> NET : Protected\nRaSTA Messages
NET --> APP_B : Verified\nApplication Data

note bottom of NET
Network is NOT trusted.
Safety is ensured by RaSTA endpoints.
end note

@enduml